From 737a68fd036f17cb803c4ee2b4973bdec111ec64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:04:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] workspace_source PR-2: secret scan reads the exact pushed
 objects in an isolated git env

Review t_01a1d4bba84dceb2 (PR #2142 @b5e2444ebb) found two more scan bypasses of the
diff-text parser: `git replace --graft` hid a commit the push still sends, and an added
line starting with `++ ` was read as a file header. Fix the class, not the parser:

- Scan objects, not unified-diff text: `rev-list --objects <head> --not <base>` lists
  exactly what the push can send; every new blob's raw bytes (`cat-file --batch`, no
  filters/textconv), every new commit's headers + message, and every new tree entry
  name (denylist + secret patterns; base (path, sha) pairs skipped). UTF-8/16/32 by
  BOM or NUL pattern; undecodable blobs are binary, scanned for PEM markers and
  printable runs.
- One isolated git env for scan and push: GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1,
  GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1, GIT_GRAFT_FILE=/dev/null,
  core.attributesFile/hooksPath=/dev/null. The push re-supplies only the user's
  credential helper for the https URL, and pushes the scanned sha.
- Tests (RED on b5e2444ebb: 10 failures): replace --graft, info/grafts, diff-header-
  shaped content lines, UTF-16/32 blobs, global hooks/attributes ignored, base-carried
  denylisted file not refused, and a 12-seed property test (random secret in a new
  blob, commit message or path name is refused and never pushed).
